Subject: [PATCH] jails/instances/lab-mail: Initial spec
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: rlrysuruvryxyvntzzsmyzxntuyxxkuv

Agents need to send and read p7x.dev mail, but the Fastmail
credentials should not live in any jail an agent works in. A
standalone spec settles what the relay jail does before anything is
built, so the design can be reviewed and changed in one place.

It records the decisions made so far: bind to loopback and rely on
inherit networking instead of pf, restrict recipients but not
senders, and pull lists/ into a local copy so that read-only access
to Fastmail holds by construction. The open questions are the ones
only the account owner can answer.
